  <!-- Stats -->
  <StatsSection stats={[
    {
      value: '2M+',
      label: 'Facebook Photos Downloaded',
      sub: 'Save FB photos in full resolution',
      icon: 'download',
    },
    {
      value: '150+',
      label: 'Countries Using Our FB Photo Saver',
      sub: 'Download Facebook photos from anywhere',
      icon: 'globe',
    },
    {
      value: '4.8',
      label: 'Free Full-Resolution Photo Downloads',
      sub: 'No watermark, no login required',
      icon: 'star',
    },
  ]} />

  <!-- SEO Content Section — 600+ words -->
  <FbSeoArticle
    headline="Download Facebook photos in full resolution — free and watermark-free."
    quickLinks={[
      { label: 'Facebook Photo Downloader', href: '#download-tool' },
      { label: 'How It Works', href: '#how-it-works' },
      { label: 'Features', href: '#features' },
      { label: 'FAQ', href: '#faq' },
      { label: 'Facebook Video Downloader', href: '/facebook-video-downloader' },
    ]}
    supportedLinks={['facebook.com/photo.php?fbid=…', 'facebook.com/{profile}/photos/…', 'Photo permalinks from the Share menu']}
  >
    <p>
      TikSaveHub is the fastest way to <strong>download Facebook photos in full resolution for free</strong>.
      Facebook heavily compresses images in your feed and limits you to right-click saving and crop-able
      screenshots — none of which give you the original file. With our <strong>Facebook photo downloader</strong>,
      you paste a photo link and get the full-resolution image the person actually uploaded: sharp, clean, and ready
      to keep forever, with no watermark and no sign-up.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-highlight">How to download a Facebook photo in full resolution</h3>
    <p>
      It takes under ten seconds. Open the photo you want to save on the Facebook app or website, tap the Share
      button and choose "Copy Link" — the URL looks like <em>facebook.com/photo.php?fbid=1234567890</em> or
      <em>facebook.com/username/photos/1234567890</em>. Come back to TikSaveHub and paste it into the input field at
      the top of this page. Hit Download Photo and our servers locate the original image on Facebook's CDN
      instantly, showing a preview with a single "Download Photo" button. One more tap and the original-resolution
      JPG or PNG lands on your device — no app, no login, no watermark.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-highlight">Why users pick TikSaveHub for Facebook photos</h3>
    <p>
      Most "photo downloader" sites redirect you through fake buttons, watermarks, or registration walls — and some
      even hand you compressed preview files instead of the original. TikSaveHub does none of that. It is a free
      online Facebook photo downloader that works in any browser on any device — <strong>download Facebook photos on
      iPhone</strong>, Android, Windows, or Mac with the exact same paste-and-download flow. Downloads are
      unlimited, your history is never stored, and the image you receive is the untouched original upload, at its
      maximum resolution.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-highlight">Full resolution — exactly as uploaded</h3>
    <p>
      When a photographer uploads a photo in 4K, our downloader delivers 4K. When the source is a smaller capture,
      you get the best size Facebook actually stores — typically up to 2048px on the side. We never re-encode, never
      compress, and never add overlays: the JPG or PNG you save is a faithful copy of the original, not a screenshot
      and not a feed preview.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-highlight">Which photos can you save?</h3>
    <p>
      Standard photo posts, profile and cover-adjacent photos shared publicly, album permalinks, and photo.php
      links all work. Best of all, the same Facebook page on TikSaveHub can handle everything else the platform
      offers — a <a href="/facebook-video-downloader">Facebook video downloader</a> for video posts and Watch
      links, <a href="/facebook-reels-downloader">Reels downloader in HD 1080p</a>, a
      <a href="/facebook-story-downloader">story downloader</a>, and a <a href="/facebook-to-mp3">Facebook to MP3
      converter</a> — so one bookmark covers all of Facebook.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-highlight">Download photos on iPhone, Android, and desktop</h3>
    <p>
      On iPhone or iPad, open Safari, paste the link and tap Download Photo — the image appears in Files under
      Downloads or in your camera roll. On Android, the photo saves straight to your gallery. On a PC or Mac, it
      lands in your browser's download bar. Everything is responsive and touch-friendly, with 48px tap targets and
      zero clutter, so it feels native no matter your screen.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-highlight">Privacy and safety — no account, no tracking</h3>
    <p>
      We do not ask for your email, we do not store your download history, and we never crawl your profile. The
      conversion happens server-side and the only thing that lands on your phone, tablet, or computer is the final
      image file. That's the TikSaveHub promise: a free, fast, and private <strong>Facebook photo downloader with no
      watermark</strong>, ready whenever you are.
    </p>

    <p>
      Want other formats too? You can also save <a href="/facebook-video-downloader">Facebook videos in HD</a>,
      grab <a href="/facebook-reels-downloader">Reels in HD 1080p</a>, convert <a href="/facebook-to-mp3">Facebook
      videos to MP3</a>, or save <a href="/facebook-story-downloader">Facebook stories</a> — all free, all without a
      watermark.
    </p>
  </FbSeoArticle>

  <!-- How It Works -->
  <FbStepsSection
    eyebrow="Step-by-Step Guide"
    headline="How to download Facebook photos."
    sub="Three simple steps — no technical skills required."
    steps={[
      {
        num: '01',
        icon: 'copy',
        title: 'Copy the photo link',
        body: 'Open the Facebook app or site, open the photo you want, tap Share, and select "Copy Link." Every public photo link format works: photo.php?fbid=…, profile photo permalinks, or album links.',
      },
      {
        num: '02',
        icon: 'paste',
        title: 'Paste it into TikSaveHub',
        body: 'Come back here and paste the link into the field above — the Paste button grabs it straight from your clipboard. We detect the photo and locate its original file in seconds.',
      },
      {
        num: '03',
        icon: 'download',
        title: 'Download full resolution',
        body: 'Tap "Download Photo" to save the image at its maximum available resolution — up to 2048px on the side. The file saves instantly — no app or account needed.',
      },
    ]}
